From: dMopp <5166587+dMopp@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] winex11, winewayland: use the exe name when SteamAppId is 0 or "default".

umu-run exports SteamAppId=default (GAMEID=umu-default, which Faugus, Lutris
and Heroic use for games without an umu database entry) or SteamAppId=0 (a
GAMEID without the umu- prefix). Every game then gets the same WM_CLASS /
app ID, steam_app_default or steam_app_0. Child processes inherit the
variable, so a launcher such as Battle.net and every game it starts (WoW,
Diablo, Overwatch ...) share one ID as well. Docks and task bars group them
under one generic icon and window rules cannot tell them apart.

Treat these placeholder values like an unset SteamAppId and fall back to the
lowercased exe name, as upstream Wine does (battle.net.exe, wow.exe). winex11
used to fall back to "steam_proton" when SteamAppId was unset; it now uses the
exe name too, matching winewayland. Real Steam app IDs are unchanged.

Refs: https://github.com/ValveSoftware/Proton/issues/9994
Refs: https://github.com/Faugus/faugus-launcher/issues/1042
---
diff --git a/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c b/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c
index cc3b6185b70..25c63d4e0f8 100644
--- a/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c
+++ b/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c
@@ -1250,10 +1250,16 @@ static void set_initial_wm_hints( Display *display, Window window )
         const char *app_id = getenv("SteamAppId");
         char proton_app_class[128];
 
-        if(app_id && *app_id){
+        /* Launchers outside of Steam (umu) export SteamAppId=0 or "default"
+         * for every game, and games started from a launcher inherit it. Use
+         * the exe name like upstream Wine then, so their windows differ. */
+        if(app_id && *app_id && strcmp(app_id, "0") && strcmp(app_id, "default")){
             snprintf(proton_app_class, sizeof(proton_app_class), "steam_app_%s", app_id);
             class_hints->res_name = proton_app_class;
             class_hints->res_class = proton_app_class;
+        }else if(process_name){
+            class_hints->res_name = process_name;
+            class_hints->res_class = process_name;
         }else{
             class_hints->res_name = steam_proton;
             class_hints->res_class = steam_proton;
--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/waylanddrv_main.c
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/waylanddrv_main.c
@@ -112,9 +112,11 @@ static void wayland_init_app_id(void)
     const char *steam_app_id = getenv("SteamAppId");
     size_t size;
 
-    /* Match the WM_CLASS winex11 sets, so games are identified the same way
-     * on Wayland and XWayland. */
-    if (steam_app_id && *steam_app_id)
+    /* Match the WM_CLASS winex11 sets, so games are identified the same way
+     * on Wayland and XWayland. SteamAppId=0 or "default" comes from launchers
+     * outside of Steam (umu) and is shared by every game they run. */
+    if (steam_app_id && *steam_app_id && strcmp(steam_app_id, "0") &&
+        strcmp(steam_app_id, "default"))
     {
         size = sizeof("steam_app_") + strlen(steam_app_id);
         if ((process_app_id = malloc(size)))
